    "description": "Okuma Corporation, together with its subsidiaries, manufactures and sells machine tools in Japan, the Americas, Europe, and the Asia-Pacific. The company offers multitasking machines; 5-axis vertical and horizontal machining centers, as well as 5-axis high-speed blade machine; saddle, parallel spindle, and vertical CNC lathes, as well as twin spindle turning centers and aluminum wheel applications; vertical and horizontal machining centers; double-column machining centers; CNC cylindrical and internal grinders; intelligent CNC, software, and IoT solution; and automation robot system. It also provides green-smart machine, collision avoidance system, and sludgeless tank; thermo-friendly concept, 5-axis auto tuning system, servo Navi, and machining Navi; gear machining package, turn-cut, flat-tool grooving, hyper-surface, dynamic tool load control, B-axis turning, and threading; auto attachment head compensation, NC gage, C-axis torque skip, ADMAC-parts, 3D virtual monitor, machine status logger/cutting status monitor, OSP-AI, OSP-VPS, and one-touch spreadsheet; and dream sites and connect plan solutions. In addition, the company engages in the provision of after-sales services; sale of maintenance parts; machining, assembly, and installation of machine tool parts; and machine tool mechanical design. It serves automotive, semiconductor, wind power generation, aircraft, medical equipment, construction machinery, and die/mold industries. The company was founded in 1898 and is headquartered in Niwa, Japan."
